  "question": {
    "text": "The edge length of a face centered cubic cell of an ionic substance is $508 \\mathrm{pm}$. If the radius of the cation is $110 \\mathrm{pm}$, the radius of the anion is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xWjte",
      "text": "\n$288 \\mathrm{pm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZrBTn",
      "text": "\n$398 \\mathrm{pm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "skB2w",
      "text": "\n$618 \\mathrm{pm}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LJTjV",
      "text": "\n$144 \\mathrm{pm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For an ionic substance in FCC arrangement,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& 2\\left(r^{+}+r^{-}\\right)=\\text {edge length } \\\\\n& 2\\left(110+r^{-}\\right)=508 \\\\\n& r^{-}=144 \\mathrm{pm}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
